@startuml
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #45627B
skinparam classBackgroundColor #EEF5FB
skinparam classBorderColor #45627B
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FAFCFE
hide empty members
title Recovery: FC command → actual OpenRocket deployment

participant "FC state action / Java board" as FC
participant RTPyroController as P
participant FlightComputerRecoveryBridge as B
participant "Basic/Modified event engine" as E
participant RecoveryDevice as D
participant FlightDataBranch as F
FC -> P : armPyro(channel); firePyro(channel, origin)
P -> P : validate arm gate; capture bootUs + sequence
P -> B : accepted FireCommand
B -> B : resolve channel → device UUID + delayUs
B -> E : enqueue FC-owned deployment event
E -> B : allow(event)?
B --> E : ownership + run/device eligibility
alt accepted and not vetoed/aborted by the engine
 E -> D : deploy physical device
 E -> B : recoveryDeployed(event)
 B -> F : actual device state + event timestamp
else rejected
 E -> B : rejectRecoveryEvent(event, reason)
end
note over B,E
FC-enabled simulations override normal deployment rules.
A logical pulse is not proof of physical deployment.
Recovery deadlines do not wait for servo PWM or radio delivery.
end note

@enduml
